s://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Ned_Rubenstein","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY":{"id":"F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","title":"Steve Christy character reference","label":"Steve Christy character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Steve_Christy","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH":{"id":"F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH","title":"Ralph Neeley character reference","label":"Ralph Neeley character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Ralph_Neeley","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-OFFICER-DORF":{"id":"F13-CHAR-OFFICER-DORF","title":"Dorf character reference","label":"Dorf character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Dorf","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-ENOS":{"id":"F13-CHAR-ENOS","title":"Enos character reference","label":"Enos character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Enos","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-BARRY":{"id":"F13-CHAR-BARRY","title":"Barry Jackson character reference","label":"Barry Jackson character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Barry_Jackson","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-CHAR-CLAUDETTE":{"id":"F13-CHAR-CLAUDETTE","title":"Claudette Hayes character reference","label":"Claudette Hayes character reference","url":"https://fridaythe13th.fandom.com/wiki/Claudette_Hayes","kind":"secondary character cross-check","note":"Only 1980 on-screen facts used. Reject novelization/game/comic background, exact ages, family inventions, unsupported surnames, later deaths and disputed 1979 chronology. Some pages retrieved through search index, not direct fetch.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-TIERNEY":{"id":"F13-TIERNEY","title":"Ronn Carroll / Sgt. Tierney retrospective","label":"Ronn Carroll / Sgt. Tierney retrospective","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/saga/part1/ronncarroll/","kind":"performer reference","note":"Credit and retrospective recollection only; historical contact information not retained.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false},"F13-DORF":{"id":"F13-DORF","title":"Officer Dorf dialogue reference","label":"Officer Dorf dialogue reference","url":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0080761/characters/nm0589798/","kind":"dialogue cross-check","note":"Supports motorcycle-police visit, search for Ralph and confrontation with counselors; not novelized police backstory.","access":"Public source reviewed 2026-10-17. Source synthesis; no complete film viewing performed.","filmFootageViewed":false,"fullIssueRead":false}}},"movieDetails":{"version":"10.50-research","movies":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"title":"Friday the 13th (1980)","overview":"A group preparing to reopen a secluded summer camp ignores its grim reputation, only to find that someone is determined to keep Crystal Lake closed.","plot":["In 1958, Camp Crystal Lake is still a place of group songs and youthful flirtation. Barry and Claudette slip away from the other counselors for privacy, only to be cornered by someone the camera will not identify. The killings make the camp’s ordinary buildings feel dangerous before the story moves forward to a new attempt at opening the property.","On Friday, June 13, Annie arrives in the nearby town expecting to become the camp’s cook. Ralph warns her to stay away, and truck driver Enos gives her a partial lift while describing a history of drowning, murders, fires and a failed reopening. She is determined to take the job. A second ride becomes threatening when the unseen driver passes the camp turnoff. Annie jumps from the vehicle, injures herself and flees into the woods, where she is killed before the other staff ever meet her.","At the camp, Steve Christy is directing repairs with Alice, Bill, Brenda, Jack, Marcie and Ned. The work shares space with swimming, flirtation and jokes. Officer Dorf’s visit and Ralph’s warning seem like interruptions rather than useful protection. Steve goes into town, while the camera repeatedly suggests someone is watching. As a storm approaches, Ned follows a figure into a cabin and vanishes. Jack and Marcie shelter together there, unaware of his body in the upper bunk. After Marcie leaves for the bathroom, Jack is killed from beneath the bed. Marcie is attacked in the washroom.","Elsewhere, Alice, Bill and Brenda spend the evening together. Brenda returns to her cabin but hears what sounds like a child needing help. She ventures outside toward the archery range, where the lights suddenly come on and a scream is heard. Alice and Bill investigate, find a bloodied axe and discover that the telephone and available vehicle cannot get them help. Steve, delayed by the weather and vehicle trouble, receives a partial lift from Sgt. Tierney. He reaches camp on foot, recognizes the person waiting there and is killed. When the camp loses power, Bill checks the generator and fails to return.","Alice discovers Bill’s body and retreats to the main cabin, where Brenda’s body is thrown through a window. Headlights initially seem to promise rescue. Instead, Mrs. Voorhees arrives, introduces herself as a friend of the Christys and tells Alice about her son Jason, who drowned while counselors were distracted. Her account becomes an accusation, revealing the killer behind the night’s attacks. Alice resists and escapes her repeatedly. At the shore, their final struggle ends when Alice takes the machete and decapitates her attacker.","Exhausted, Alice pushes away from shore in a canoe. Morning seems to bring safety, until a disfigured boy bursts from the lake and pulls her toward the water. She abruptly wakes in a hospital. Tierney tells her the others are dead but that police found no boy. The film returns to the quiet lake rather than supplying an explanation. Alice survives the human killer; whether the final child attack is a nightmare, an apparition or something else remains unsettled within this film."],"plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","spoiler":true,"continuity":"The foundation film of the original Friday the 13th series. This dossier covers the original 1980 theatrical story only; later sequels, remakes and spin-offs remain outside its character accounts.","keyEvents":[{"title":"1957 · the drowning","detail":"Enos recalls a boy drowning. Mrs. Voorhees later identifies that boy as Jason and blames inattentive counselors.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"1958 · the opening murders","detail":"Barry and Claudette are killed at camp. The film does not establish that they were the specific counselors supervising Jason in 1957.","sourceIds":["F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"Before the reopening · fires and bad water","detail":"Enos mentions fires and a 1962 reopening prevented by bad water. Do not assign a precise year to every fire or invent a complete sabotage chronology.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"title":"Friday, June 13 · preparations","detail":"Annie travels toward camp while Steve and the counselors make repairs. The exact contemporary year is left qualified in this dossier.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"title":"Stormy night · isolation","detail":"The staff are attacked separately. Normal routes to help fail; Steve and Bill do not return to aid Alice.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"The reveal · Mrs. Voorhees","detail":"Her account of Jason’s death reveals the motive behind the attacks; Alice ultimately kills her at the shore.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-PLOT"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"Morning and hospital · unresolved boy","detail":"The canoe attack is followed by Alice’s hospital awakening and the report that police found no boy.","sourceIds":["F13-LEHMAN","F13-PLOT"],"spoiler":true}],"timeline":[{"title":"1957 · the drowning","detail":"Enos recalls a boy drowning. Mrs. Voorhees later identifies that boy as Jason and blames inattentive counselors.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"1958 · the opening murders","detail":"Barry and Claudette are killed at camp. The film does not establish that they were the specific counselors supervising Jason in 1957.","sourceIds":["F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"Before the reopening · fires and bad water","detail":"Enos mentions fires and a 1962 reopening prevented by bad water. Do not assign a precise year to every fire or invent a complete sabotage chronology.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"title":"Friday, June 13 · preparations","detail":"Annie travels toward camp while Steve and the counselors make repairs. The exact contemporary year is left qualified in this dossier.","sourceIds":["F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"title":"Stormy night · isolation","detail":"The staff are attacked separately. Normal routes to help fail; Steve and Bill do not return to aid Alice.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"The reveal · Mrs. Voorhees","detail":"Her account of Jason’s death reveals the motive behind the attacks; Alice ultimately kills her at the shore.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-PLOT"],"spoiler":true},{"title":"Morning and hospital · unresolved boy","detail":"The canoe attack is followed by Alice’s hospital awakening and the report that police found no boy.","sourceIds":["F13-LEHMAN","F13-PLOT"],"spoiler":true}],"locations":[{"name":"Camp Crystal Lake","detail":"Fictional camp with cabins, an archery range, utility buildings and a lake. Real filming location: Camp No-Be-Bo-Sco."},{"name":"Nearby town and roads","detail":"Annie’s journey and Steve’s errands connect the camp to an outside world that remains too distant to prevent the attacks."},{"name":"Hospital","detail":"Alice’s final conversation with police; exact building location is not established by the sources used here."}],"connections":[{"title":"Franchise foundation","detail":"The Voorhees family and Crystal Lake become the continuing series’ central names, but this film’s threat is specifically the mother’s revenge.","sourceIds":["F13-CREDITS","F13-MILLER"]},{"title":"Next film: Friday the 13th Part 2 (1981)","detail":"The sequel continues the original series. Its later Jason premise and other characters’ subsequent fates are deliberately kept outside these 1980 dossiers.","sourceIds":["F13-PART2"]},{"title":"Halloween influence, not shared universe","detail":"Creator accounts identify Halloween’s success as a model for the production. That creative connection does not place Michael Myers or Haddonfield inside Friday the 13th continuity.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-LEHMAN"]},{"title":"The final shock and Carrie","detail":"Creator recollections connect the last surprise to the tradition of Carrie’s apparent ending giving way to one more nightmare. Accounts differ over who originated each element, so no single person is credited here as its uncontested sole inventor.","sourceIds":["F13-SAVINI","F13-LEHMAN"]}],"sources":[{"title":"AFI Catalog: Friday the 13th (1980)","label":"AFI Catalog: Friday the 13th (1980)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56417-FRIDAY-THE-13TH"},{"title":"Paramount Pictures: Friday the 13th","label":"Paramount Pictures: Friday the 13th","url":"https://www.paramountpictures.com/movies/friday-the-13th"},{"title":"Friday the 13th: original cast and crew transcription","label":"Friday the 13th: original cast and crew transcription","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/saga/cast_crew1/"},{"title":"Friday the 13th dialogue continuity","label":"Friday the 13th dialogue continuity","url":"https://fridaythe13thlegacy.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Friday-The-13th-1980-Script.pdf"},{"title":"Friday the 13th (1980 film): plot cross-check","label":"Friday the 13th (1980 film): plot cross-check","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friday_the_13th_(1980_film)"},{"title":"Friday the 13th (1980): story reference","label":"Friday the 13th (1980): story reference","url":"https://horror.fandom.com/wiki/Friday_the_13th_(1980)"},{"title":"Victor Miller interview","label":"Victor Miller interview","url":"https://indiemacuser.com/2015/06/23/horror-month-interview-with-victor-miller/"},{"title":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","label":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","url":"https://crystallaketours.com/visit/"},{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"},{"title":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","label":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","url":"https://visitnj.org/trail-itinerary/friday-13th"},{"title":"Blairstown Diner: Our Story","label":"Blairstown Diner: Our Story","url":"https://www.blairstowndiner.com/history"},{"title":"Harry Manfredini interview: A Conversation About Friday the 13th","label":"Harry Manfredini interview: A Conversation About Friday the 13th","url":"https://www.frightday.com/a-conversation-with-composer-harry-manfredini-about-friday-the-13th/"},{"title":"Ari Lehman interview, hosted by First Jason","label":"Ari Lehman interview, hosted by First Jason","url":"https://firstjason.com/news-history/blog/6050758/interview-ari-lehman-jason-voorhees-friday-the-13th-1980"},{"title":"IMP Awards: original Friday the 13th theatrical poster","label":"IMP Awards: original Friday the 13th theatrical poster","url":"https://www.impawards.com/1980/friday_the_thirteenth.html"}],"cast":[{"name":"Alice","actor":"Adrienne King","slug":"friday13-alice","creditedAs":"Alice"},{"name":"Mrs. Voorhees","actor":"Betsy Palmer","slug":"friday13-mrs-voorhees","creditedAs":"Mrs. Voorhees"},{"name":"Jason Voorhees","actor":"Ari Lehman","slug":"friday13-jason","creditedAs":"Jason"},{"name":"Annie","actor":"Robbi Morgan","slug":"friday13-annie","creditedAs":"Annie"},{"name":"Jack","actor":"Kevin Bacon","slug":"friday13-jack","creditedAs":"Jack"},{"name":"Marcie","actor":"Jeannine Taylor","slug":"friday13-marcie","creditedAs":"Marcie"},{"name":"Bill","actor":"Harry Crosby","slug":"friday13-bill","creditedAs":"Bill"},{"name":"Brenda","actor":"Laurie Bartram","slug":"friday13-brenda","creditedAs":"Brenda"},{"name":"Ned","actor":"Mark Nelson","slug":"friday13-ned","creditedAs":"Ned"},{"name":"Steve Christy","actor":"Peter Brouwer","slug":"friday13-steve-christy","creditedAs":"Steve Christy"},{"name":"Crazy Ralph","actor":"Walt Gorney","slug":"friday13-crazy-ralph","creditedAs":"Crazy Ralph"},{"name":"Officer Dorf","actor":"Ron Millkie","slug":"friday13-officer-dorf","creditedAs":"Officer Dorf"},{"name":"Sgt. Tierney","actor":"Ronn Carroll","slug":"friday13-sgt-tierney","creditedAs":"Sgt. Tierney"},{"name":"Enos","actor":"Rex Everhart","slug":"friday13-enos","creditedAs":"The Truck Driver"},{"name":"Barry","actor":"Willie Adams","slug":"friday13-barry","creditedAs":"Barry"},{"name":"Claudette","actor":"Debra S. Hayes","slug":"friday13-claudette","creditedAs":"Claudette"}],"castLabel":"16 core named characters · original film","triviaFilmId":"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical","sourcePolicy":"Original, spoiler-gated synthesis of film-credit and dialogue records with creator interviews and labeled secondary checks. No full-film viewing claimed. First names follow 1980 credits; alias and year discrepancies remain visible. Supporting credited locals and generic roles are not all cataloged as individual dossiers.","credits":{"releaseYear":1980,"releaseDateUS":"1980-05-09","director":"Sean S. Cunningham","screenplay":["Victor Miller"],"producer":"Sean S. Cunningham","associateProducer":"Steve Miner","cinematography":"Barry Abrams","editor":"Bill Freda","music":"Harry Manfredini","specialMakeupEffects":"Tom Savini","productionCompany":"Georgetown Productions","distributorUS":"Paramount Pictures","country":"United States","language":"English","runtimeMinutes":95,"ratingUS":"R","edition":"Original theatrical release","sourceIds":["F13-AFI","F13-CREDITS"],"producers":["Sean S. Cunningham","Steve Miner (associate producer)"],"distributor":"Paramount Pictures"},"runtimeNote":"95 minutes follows AFI’s theatrical catalog. Some home-video/distribution listings round to 96; Paramount’s current web field of 120 is not used.","financials":{"currency":"USD","productionBudgetReported":650000,"domesticBoxOfficeReported":39754601,"internationalBoxOfficeReported":20000000,"worldwideBoxOfficeReported":59754601,"sourceIds":["F13-NUMBERS"],"note":"Reported historical figures; not adjusted for inflation and not a profit calculation."},"realFilmingLocations":{"researchedAt":"2026-10-17","editorialNote":"Selected actual filming sites are separate from fictional geography. Official current access rules supersede old fan travel accounts. No private residence addresses are included. A scene-matched structure is not a promise of unchanged interiors or visitor admission.","locations":[{"name":"Camp No-Be-Bo-Sco","city":"Hardwick Township","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Camp Crystal Lake","scenes":"The central campground: wooded approaches, cabins and much of the counselors’ work and night-time danger.","filmingUse":"Real working camp and grounds","siteType":"Private youth camp","statusNote":"The official tour operator identifies the camp as the primary 1979 filming location and says over 80 percent of the film was made there.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","label":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","url":"https://crystallaketours.com/visit/"},{"title":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","label":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","url":"https://visitnj.org/trail-itinerary/friday-13th"}],"uncertainties":"Do not confuse Hardwick Township with the Blairstown postal/location shorthand or assume later franchise films used this same camp.","accessNote":"Active private youth camp. The official operator prohibits visits outside its scheduled tours. A roadside arrival or film-fan interest is not permission to enter. Tour inclusions vary."},{"name":"Van Dusen cabin / main cabin","city":"Hardwick Township","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Camp’s main lodge and kitchen","scenes":"The evening game, Alice’s barricade and the encounter with Mrs. Voorhees.","filmingUse":"Cabin interior and immediate exterior","siteType":"Building within private camp","statusNote":"Scene-comparison photographs identify this structure as Van Dusen cabin.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"}],"uncertainties":"Building nomenclature may differ in modern tour materials; do not promise a specific interior is open.","accessNote":"Active private youth camp. The official operator prohibits visits outside its scheduled tours. A roadside arrival or film-fan interest is not permission to enter. Tour inclusions vary."},{"name":"Mechanics / generator building","city":"Hardwick Township","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Camp generator shed","scenes":"Bill checks the failed power; Alice later finds him at the building.","filmingUse":"Existing service building","siteType":"Utility structure within private camp","statusNote":"The comparison archive identifies the building and its generator-related use.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"}],"uncertainties":"Exact present-day equipment and access are not verified.","accessNote":"Active private youth camp. The official operator prohibits visits outside its scheduled tours. A roadside arrival or film-fan interest is not permission to enter. Tour inclusions vary."},{"name":"Sand Pond waterfront","city":"Hardwick Township","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Crystal Lake","scenes":"Swimming, waterfront conversations, the final shore struggle and canoe ending.","filmingUse":"Lake, shore and dock area","siteType":"Waterfront within private camp","statusNote":"Sand Pond is the real body of water used for the original film’s lake.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"},{"title":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","label":"Crystal Lake Tours: Visit the Original Camp Crystal Lake","url":"https://crystallaketours.com/visit/"}],"uncertainties":"Dock positions and seasonal structures can change. The depicted lake and fictional geography are not a precise map.","accessNote":"Active private youth camp. The official operator prohibits visits outside its scheduled tours. A roadside arrival or film-fan interest is not permission to enter. Tour inclusions vary."},{"name":"Camp archery range","city":"Hardwick Township","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Crystal Lake archery area","scenes":"Brenda works on the range; the night-time call for help draws her back there.","filmingUse":"Outdoor activity area","siteType":"Grounds within private camp","statusNote":"Scene-comparison images document the range as a film location.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"}],"uncertainties":"Modern clearance and equipment may differ; do not infer the exact off-screen method of Brenda’s death.","accessNote":"Active private youth camp. The official operator prohibits visits outside its scheduled tours. A roadside arrival or film-fan interest is not permission to enter. Tour inclusions vary."},{"name":"Old Mill archways, footbridge and Main Street","city":"Blairstown","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Town near Camp Crystal Lake","scenes":"Annie’s walk into town after the prologue.","filmingUse":"Street exteriors and pedestrian structures","siteType":"Public streets beside historic/private buildings","statusNote":"The opening route uses recognizable town landmarks; Roy’s Hall also appears among the town views.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"},{"title":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","label":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","url":"https://visitnj.org/trail-itinerary/friday-13th"}],"uncertainties":"Separate the filmed exterior storefront from the shop interior in Hope.","accessNote":"Use public walkways where permitted. Adjacent buildings and businesses retain their own access rules; avoid blocking traffic or entrances."},{"name":"Hartung’s store / shop interior","city":"Hope","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"The shop/café where Annie asks directions","scenes":"Annie speaks with local people and arranges the first ride.","filmingUse":"Interior distinct from Blairstown storefront exterior","siteType":"Historic commercial filming site","statusNote":"Location archive distinguishes the Hope interior from the Blairstown exterior.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"}],"uncertainties":"Current business identity, interior survival and visitor access have not been verified; no current street-number claim is made.","accessNote":"Filming history does not grant access. Follow current site rules and do not enter private or restricted areas."},{"name":"Blairstown Diner","city":"Blairstown","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"The diner visited by Steve","scenes":"Steve’s evening stop and conversation with waitress Sandy.","filmingUse":"Working diner interior/exterior","siteType":"Public business","statusNote":"The operator identifies its original-film connection and address as 53 NJ-94, Blairstown.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Blairstown Diner: Our Story","label":"Blairstown Diner: Our Story","url":"https://www.blairstowndiner.com/history"},{"title":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","label":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","url":"https://visitnj.org/trail-itinerary/friday-13th"}],"uncertainties":"This is Steve’s diner scene, not the Hope shop interior where Annie asks for directions. Hours and special events require a fresh check.","accessNote":"Visit only during the business’s normal service or authorized events. A meal or public visit does not authorize filming equipment or access behind the counter."},{"name":"Hope Moravian Cemetery roadside","city":"Hope","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Crossroads along Annie’s journey","scenes":"Enos drops Annie off nearby before she seeks her second ride.","filmingUse":"Roadside exterior","siteType":"Cemetery setting / public-road approach","statusNote":"New Jersey tourism lists Hope Moravian Cemetery as a film-trail stop.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","label":"New Jersey tourism: Friday the 13th film trail","url":"https://visitnj.org/trail-itinerary/friday-13th"},{"title":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","label":"Friday the 13th filming-location comparison archive","url":"https://fridaythe13thfilms.com/bts/locations/part1/"}],"uncertainties":"The scene’s apparent proximity to camp is edited geography, not a reliable route.","accessNote":"Respect cemetery rules, mourners and traffic. The filming connection is not permission to enter restricted grounds or stand in the road."},{"name":"Roy’s Hall","city":"Blairstown","region":"New Jersey, USA","fictionalPlace":"Town street landmark","scenes":"Seen in the town’s opening travel views.","filmingUse":"Background exterior landmark","siteType":"Historic theater","statusNote":"Blair Academy’s local history identifies Roy’s Hall among the recognizable landmarks.","statusAsOf":"Sources reviewed 2026-10-17","sources":[{"title":"Blair Academy: Legends & Lore of Blair, filming Friday the 13th","label":"Blair Academy: Legends & Lore of Blair, filming Friday the 13th","url":"https://www.blair.edu/about-blair/publications-news/post/~board/news/post/legends-lore-of-blair-part-7-the-filming-of-friday-the-13th"}],"uncertainties":"An exterior appearance does not mean any theater interior was used.","accessNote":"View from public areas or attend an authorized event; do not assume unrestricted interior access."}],"unverifiedCandidates":[{"name":"Freehold / final hospital scene","note":"Some location indexes name Freehold, but no sufficiently reliable building-level identification was established in this pass. Do not invent a hospital name or address."}]},"continuityWarnings":["Do not identify Jason as the murderer of the 1980 staff.","Do not add adult Jason, a hockey mask, a sack mask or sequel powers to the child dossier.","Do not mark Alice or Ralph dead on the strength of later films.","Do not claim Brenda’s precise off-screen death method.","Do not state Barry and Claudette definitely caused Jason’s drowning.","Do not treat production year, release year and disputed story year as interchangeable."],"poster":{"sourcePage":"https://www.impawards.com/1980/friday_the_thirteenth_xxlg.html","sourceImage":"https://www.impawards.com/1980/posters/friday_the_thirteenth_xxlg.jpg","file":"/workspace/shared/friday-1980-research/friday-the-13th-1980-original-theatrical-poster.jpg","sha256":"2055186d1bc2062c032ecde89dd3330d9bbe7fde62c044dc3ea6fcc075a8be6f","transformation":"None; original downloaded JPEG","artwork":"Original U.S. theatrical one-sheet illustration by Alex Ebel; archive describes official theatrical poster","nativeDimensions":"1949x2906, per source metadata; confirm locally","cover":"movie-covers/friday-the-13th-1980.jpg"},"releaseDate":"1980-05-09 (United States)","runtime":"95 minutes · theatrical catalog","editionNotes":["95 minutes follows AFI’s theatrical catalog. Some home-video/distribution listings round to 96; Paramount’s current web field of 120 is not used."],"continuityDetails":"The foundation film of the original Friday the 13th series. Only the 1980 theatrical narrative is described here. Mrs. Voorhees is the killer; child Jason’s final appearance is dream-framed and unresolved. No adult hockey mask, later resurrection rules, sequel deaths, remake or television-prequel biography is imported.","connectionsSpoilers":true}},"characterSnapshots":{"friday13-alice":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Alice can draw, has sketched Steve, and is uncertain whether to remain at camp. She mentions unfinished business in California but does not explain it. Steve persuades her to stay another week; the film suggests intimacy without defining their entire relationship."],"role":["Alice can draw, has sketched Steve, and is uncertain whether to remain at camp. She mentions unfinished business in California but does not explain it. Steve persuades her to stay another week; the film suggests intimacy without defining their entire relationship.","She works alongside Bill and Brenda, joins their evening game and grows alarmed when the camp’s ordinary routines stop making sense. Missing friends, a bloodied axe, a dead telephone and an unusable vehicle turn an isolated workplace into a trap. Bill’s disappearance leaves her without her last companion.","After finding Bill’s body and seeing Brenda’s body thrown through a window, Alice initially welcomes Mrs. Voorhees as an adult who might help. That apparent refuge collapses when the woman explains Jason’s death and attacks her. Alice escapes repeated confrontations and finally beheads her attacker with a machete at the shore. She drifts out in a canoe; after an apparent attack by a boy from the lake, she wakes in hospital and learns police found no boy."],"status":"Alive in hospital; traumatized; the lake encounter remains unresolved","abilities":[{"title":"Improvised defense","detail":"Uses available camp objects and turns a weapon against her attacker. No formal combat training is established.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Drawing","detail":"Her sketchbook and exchange with Steve establish an artistic interest.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Persistence under threat","detail":"Continues resisting and searching for escape despite fear and isolation.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Sketchbook","type":"Personal object","detail":"Evidence of her artistic interest.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"name":"Improvised defensive objects","type":"Situational tools","detail":"Uses objects available around camp; the machete belongs to the final confrontation, not a permanent signature arsenal.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"In the nighttime cabin sequence, Alice wears an ivory button-front blouse with narrow decorative trim and dark-brown trousers. Her short feathered strawberry-blond hair and wristwatch are visible in the inspected film references.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ALICE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-mrs-voorhees":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["She identifies Jason as her son and says he drowned because counselors were distracted instead of watching him. This is her account of the earlier tragedy, not an objective demonstration that every counselor she attacks was involved. The film supplies no husband biography, occult ritual or medical diagnosis."],"role":["She identifies Jason as her son and says he drowned because counselors were distracted instead of watching him. This is her account of the earlier tragedy, not an objective demonstration that every counselor she attacks was involved. The film supplies no husband biography, occult ritual or medical diagnosis.","Her identity is concealed during the murders. She targets people connected with the reopening, moving through the grounds and manipulating the staff’s isolation. When she finally meets Alice, she presents herself as a friend of the Christys and briefly appears to offer safety.","Her recollection of Jason becomes accusatory and violent. She speaks in a childlike voice as well as her own, acting as though her son urges her on. Alice becomes the focus of her pursuit despite having no responsibility for the old drowning. After a series of struggles, Mrs. Voorhees is decapitated at the lakeshore."],"status":"Killed by Alice in the final lakeside struggle","abilities":[{"title":"Concealment and ambush","detail":"Waits for isolated targets and uses the camp environment against them.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Deception","detail":"Initially presents herself as a helpful adult and knows the camp’s history.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Conventional violence","detail":"Employs ordinary blades and camp equipment; supernatural strength is not established.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Hunting knife and other camp weapons","type":"Conventional weapons","detail":"Weapons used in attacks; not magical artifacts.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"name":"Jeep","type":"Transport","detail":"Associated with the roadside pickup and arrival at camp.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Mrs. Voorhees has short ash-blond hair and wears a pale blue-gray cable-knit sweater over a dark high-neck layer, with dark trousers.","sourceIds":["F13-MILLER","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-jason":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["The camp’s history includes a boy’s drowning in 1957. Mrs. Voorhees identifies that child as Jason and blames inattentive counselors. Her memories and claims tell the audience what he means to her; the film does not give him an independent adult biography."],"role":["The camp’s history includes a boy’s drowning in 1957. Mrs. Voorhees identifies that child as Jason and blames inattentive counselors. Her memories and claims tell the audience what he means to her; the film does not give him an independent adult biography.","A boy struggling in water is associated with his mother’s account. The finale appears to show a misshapen, mud-covered child dragging Alice from her canoe. The immediate transition to Alice waking in a hospital makes the scene function as a nightmare shock.","When Alice asks police about the boy, they say none was found. The last image of the lake sustains unease without explaining the event. Writer Victor Miller and effects artist Tom Savini described a dead child and dream-ending conception, but the released ending leaves room for uncertainty rather than proving how a later adult Jason could exist."],"status":"Reported drowned in 1957; final lake appearance not corroborated by police","abilities":[{"title":"Ambiguous lake attack","detail":"The ending depicts a sudden grab from the water. Because it is dream-framed and uncorroborated, it is not a reliable measure of strength or survival ability.","sourceIds":["F13-LEHMAN","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[],"costume":"The ending depicts a child Jason played by Ari Lehman, emerging from the lake with the original asymmetrical prosthetic appearance. This is the ambiguous ending apparition, not the later adult, hockey-masked Jason.","sourceIds":["F13-LEHMAN","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-annie":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Hired to cook for the camp, Annie talks about wanting to work with children. She walks into town, asks for directions and accepts a lift from Enos. Her conversation makes the job feel like an opportunity rather than a dare."],"role":["Hired to cook for the camp, Annie talks about wanting to work with children. She walks into town, asks for directions and accepts a lift from Enos. Her conversation makes the job feel like an opportunity rather than a dare.","Ralph warns her, and Enos outlines the camp’s history of death and failed reopenings. Annie declines to abandon the job. After he drops her near the crossroads, another driver offers a ride. When that vehicle passes the camp turnoff and will not stop, she jumps clear and tries to escape through the woods.","Her injured leg impedes her flight, and the concealed attacker kills her with a knife. The other staff never receive the cook they are expecting. Alice later encounters her body in the vehicle during the finale."],"status":"Killed before reaching Camp Crystal Lake","abilities":[{"title":"Practical independence","detail":"Travels on foot and arranges lifts to a remote job.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ANNIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Escape attempt","detail":"Recognizes the threatening detour and acts to leave the vehicle.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ANNIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Backpack","type":"Travel equipment","detail":"Carries her belongings on the way to the camp.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ANNIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Annie arrives in a plaid overshirt over orange, a sweatshirt tied around her waist and indigo jeans, carrying an external-frame hiking backpack.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ANNIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-jack":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Jack comes to Camp Crystal Lake with his girlfriend Marcie and friend Ned. He helps Steve with the physical work and joins the group’s downtime. The film does not supply a family history or specialist trade."],"role":["Jack comes to Camp Crystal Lake with his girlfriend Marcie and friend Ned. He helps Steve with the physical work and joins the group’s downtime. The film does not supply a family history or specialist trade.","As the weather worsens, he listens to Marcie describe a recurring frightening dream. They retreat to a cabin and have sex, unaware that Ned’s body lies in the bunk above. When Marcie leaves for the bathroom, Jack remains on the bed.","Blood from above alerts him too late. The killer attacks from beneath the mattress with an arrow, turning the apparently safe sleeping space into the site of an ambush. His death is a concealed-position attack, not a fight with adult Jason."],"status":"Killed in the cabin bunk","abilities":[{"title":"Camp labor","detail":"Helps with physical preparation of the grounds.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-JACK","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Ordinary outdoor familiarity","detail":"Recognizes an approaching storm; no survival-expert credentials are established.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-JACK","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[],"costume":"In the lakeside sequence, Jack wears a pale blue checked button-up shirt with rolled sleeves over a dark olive T-shirt, with indigo jeans. His hair is sandy-brown and feathered.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-JACK","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-marcie":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["She arrives with Jack and Ned to help Steve restore the camp. The group’s jokes and leisure establish her as part of a preexisting friendship, not simply an isolated target."],"role":["She arrives with Jack and Ned to help Steve restore the camp. The group’s jokes and leisure establish her as part of a preexisting friendship, not simply an isolated target.","By the lake she tells Jack about a recurring dream in which rain becomes blood. They shelter from the storm in a cabin. Afterward she walks to the bathroom wearing a loose shirt, leaving Jack behind.","Noises draw her attention through the washroom. The hidden attacker kills her with an axe. She does not learn Jack’s fate, and the film does not show her dream functioning as a controllable supernatural ability."],"status":"Killed in the washroom","abilities":[{"title":"Ordinary camp work","detail":"Participates in preparing the property; no specialist skill or combat training is established.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-MARCIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[],"costume":"Marcie’s daytime camp outfit includes a dusty-pink short-sleeved T-shirt and high-waisted brown corduroy trousers. Her brown hair falls to about shoulder length.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-MARCIE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-bill":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Bill is already helping refurbish the camp when Jack, Marcie and Ned arrive. His painting and maintenance work mark him as useful around the grounds. He also plays guitar; no professional musician or electrician credentials are stated."],"role":["Bill is already helping refurbish the camp when Jack, Marcie and Ned arrive. His painting and maintenance work mark him as useful around the grounds. He also plays guitar; no professional musician or electrician credentials are stated.","He spends the stormy evening with Alice and Brenda. When their friends disappear, he searches with Alice, discovers that normal ways to get help are unavailable and advises waiting for Steve rather than walking through the dark countryside.","When the power fails, Bill goes to the generator building. He does not return. Alice later finds his body fixed to a door with arrows, confirming that the earlier signs were not merely a prank. The lethal attack itself is not staged as a visible fight."],"status":"Killed near the generator building; found by Alice","abilities":[{"title":"Maintenance familiarity","detail":"Paints and checks the generator; specific qualifications are unknown.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Guitar playing","detail":"A leisure skill shown in camp life.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Cooperative problem solving","detail":"Searches with Alice and tries to restore basic camp services.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Guitar","type":"Leisure instrument","detail":"Used during downtime.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"name":"Camp maintenance tools","type":"Work tools","detail":"Associated with repair duties, not a specialized combat loadout.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Bill’s red, green and white plaid shirt is visible in the original lantern-scene reference.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BILL","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-brenda":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Brenda is helping set up the camp’s archery range. Ned’s unsafe teasing irritates her, and his staged drowning provokes a genuine rescue response before he reveals the prank. Her behavior establishes concern as well as a sense of humor."],"role":["Brenda is helping set up the camp’s archery range. Ned’s unsafe teasing irritates her, and his staged drowning provokes a genuine rescue response before he reveals the prank. Her behavior establishes concern as well as a sense of humor.","During the storm she shares a game with Alice and Bill, then returns to her cabin. A childlike call for help brings her back outside with a flashlight. She follows it toward the archery range, where floodlights suddenly expose her and a scream is heard.","The film withholds the actual killing method. Her body later crashes through the main cabin’s window, terrorizing Alice. Do not label an arrow stabbing or other precise cause of death as an on-screen fact."],"status":"Killed off screen; body later thrown through the cabin window","abilities":[{"title":"Camp preparation","detail":"Works on the archery area; exact instructor credentials are not established.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Readiness to help","detail":"Responds to apparent drowning and later to a cry of distress.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Flashlight","type":"Practical tool","detail":"Carries it while searching in the storm.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"During the daytime archery sequence, Brenda wears a blue shirt tied at the waist over a red-striped white tank top, with red shorts.","sourceIds":["F13-FILM","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-ned":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Ned travels to camp with Jack and Marcie and introduces himself as Ned Rubenstein. He flirts, performs jokes and pushes at the patience of Brenda and Officer Dorf. No later family or educational history is supplied in the film."],"role":["Ned travels to camp with Jack and Marcie and introduces himself as Ned Rubenstein. He flirts, performs jokes and pushes at the patience of Brenda and Officer Dorf. No later family or educational history is supplied in the film.","His prank at the archery area is unsafe, and he fakes drowning to provoke attention and a rescue. The others’ annoyance matters because the film repeatedly allows disturbing behavior to be dismissed as joking.","Later he sees a figure enter a cabin and follows. His murder takes place off screen. The audience next sees his body in the top bunk while Jack and Marcie remain unaware below, shifting Ned from the source of false alarms to evidence of a real attack."],"status":"Killed off screen; body concealed in an upper bunk","abilities":[{"title":"Impressions and comic performance","detail":"Uses voices and broad gestures to entertain or provoke his companions.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-NED","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Ordinary swimming","detail":"Present in the lake sequence; the fake drowning is a prank, not evidence of inability to swim.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-NED","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[],"costume":"Original camp-cabin stills show Ned in a blue number-88 sports jersey with striped sleeves and pale denim cutoffs.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-NED","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-steve-christy":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["The camp is connected to the Christy family, and Enos says Steve has spent considerable time and money repairing it. Steve assigns work, hires the new staff and encourages Alice to stay despite her doubts. Precise parental names and other family details from later material are outside this film."],"role":["The camp is connected to the Christy family, and Enos says Steve has spent considerable time and money repairing it. Steve assigns work, hires the new staff and encourages Alice to stay despite her doubts. Precise parental names and other family details from later material are outside this film.","He leaves the counselors working while he goes into town. In the evening he stops at the Blairstown diner. Vehicle trouble and the storm complicate his return, and Sgt. Tierney offers him a ride before a police call diverts the officer.","Steve walks the remaining stretch and encounters someone he recognizes at the camp. His familiarity briefly makes the meeting seem harmless; the person attacks him. Alice later finds his body, confirming that the person she had been waiting for cannot rescue her."],"status":"Killed on returning to camp","abilities":[{"title":"Organization","detail":"Directs repairs and assigns work across the grounds.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Manual work","detail":"Participates in physical restoration rather than only supervising.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Jeep","type":"Transport","detail":"Used on his errands; trouble with the vehicle delays his return.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"name":"Camp work tools","type":"Work equipment","detail":"Part of his effort to restore the property.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Steve’s daytime camp-restoration appearance includes curly blond-brown hair, glasses, a mustache, bare torso, a neck bandanna and belted denim cutoffs.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-STEVE-CHRISTY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-crazy-ralph":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["The townspeople and police already know Ralph. He approaches Annie as she heads toward camp and warns that she will not return. Enos objects to his behavior even while sharing concern about the camp."],"role":["The townspeople and police already know Ralph. He approaches Annie as she heads toward camp and warns that she will not return. Enos objects to his behavior even while sharing concern about the camp.","Officer Dorf later visits the counselors looking for Ralph. Ralph himself appears from the camp pantry, startles Alice and repeats his warning before leaving on a bicycle. He does not lead a rescue or expose the killer’s identity.","The film leaves him alive. His later fate, expanded surname and any invented private knowledge about Mrs. Voorhees must not be inserted into this original-film dossier."],"status":"Alive at his final appearance in this film","abilities":[{"title":"Knowledge of local reputation","detail":"Understands that the camp’s history is dangerous or feared; he does not supply a verified investigation.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Persistence","detail":"Continues warning newcomers despite ridicule and police attention.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Bicycle","type":"Transport","detail":"Leaves the camp by bicycle.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Crazy Ralph wears a brimmed hat, striped shirt, waistcoat and brown trousers in the inspected original-film references.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-CRAZY-RALPH","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-officer-dorf":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Dorf arrives on a police motorcycle seeking Ralph. He is brusque and skeptical of the young staff, treating their jokes as a challenge to his authority. No prior big-city career is established on screen."],"role":["Dorf arrives on a police motorcycle seeking Ralph. He is brusque and skeptical of the young staff, treating their jokes as a challenge to his authority. No prior big-city career is established on screen.","Ned provokes him, and Dorf questions the group about drug use. He explains his frustration with Ralph’s public disturbances, then warns the counselors to stay out of trouble and leaves.","His visit creates a brief possibility of outside protection, but it ends before the murders are understood. He is not shown killed, solving the case or discovering a supernatural explanation."],"status":"Alive at his final appearance in this film","abilities":[{"title":"Police duties","detail":"Questioning and patrol are evident; no particular combat feat is shown.","sourceIds":["F13-DORF","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Motorcycle patrol","detail":"Uses a police motorcycle in his scene.","sourceIds":["F13-DORF","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Police motorcycle","type":"Transport","detail":"Defines the patrol visit.","sourceIds":["F13-DORF","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]},{"name":"Uniform and duty belt","type":"Professional equipment","detail":"Use original 1980 references; do not add modern tactical accessories.","sourceIds":["F13-DORF","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"The inspected original-film patrol frame shows Officer Dorf in a police helmet and an open navy jacket over a blue uniform shirt.","sourceIds":["F13-DORF","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-sgt-tierney":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["Tierney is a local police sergeant encountered during Steve’s storm-delayed return. Unlike Dorf’s earlier confrontation, his interaction with Steve is conversational and practical."],"role":["Tierney is a local police sergeant encountered during Steve’s storm-delayed return. Unlike Dorf’s earlier confrontation, his interaction with Steve is conversational and practical.","He gives Steve a ride, but a radio call requires him to leave Steve near the camp rather than escort him all the way. The audience sees how an ordinary competing duty can leave the property isolated at the critical moment.","After Alice survives, Tierney speaks to her in hospital. Asked about the boy from the water, he says no boy was found. That is the limit of his evidence: it does not prove the lake attack happened, and it does not settle Alice’s experience by diagnosing it."],"status":"Alive at the hospital aftermath","abilities":[{"title":"Police patrol and response","detail":"Responds to a dispatch and later communicates the findings to a survivor.","sourceIds":["F13-TIERNEY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Patrol car and radio","type":"Professional equipment","detail":"Used during Steve’s journey back to camp.","sourceIds":["F13-TIERNEY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"The hospital sequence shows Sgt. Tierney in a long-sleeved blue police shirt and black tie.","sourceIds":["F13-TIERNEY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-enos":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["He meets Annie at the town’s shop/café and agrees to drive her part of the way. Though he dismisses Ralph’s public outburst, he does not dismiss the camp’s history. His manner mixes teasing with genuine concern."],"role":["He meets Annie at the town’s shop/café and agrees to drive her part of the way. Though he dismisses Ralph’s public outburst, he does not dismiss the camp’s history. His manner mixes teasing with genuine concern.","During the ride he recalls the 1957 drowning, 1958 murders, fires and a reopening stopped by bad water in 1962. He also describes Steve’s investment and warns that the project may ruin him. Annie remains enthusiastic.","He drops her at the crossroads near the cemetery and continues on his route. The film does not depict him participating in the murders or secretly knowing the killer. Enos is the dialogue-continuity spelling; the screen credit calls him the truck driver and AFI brackets the spelling Ennis."],"status":"Alive when he drops Annie off","abilities":[{"title":"Driving and route knowledge","detail":"Can take Annie partway and explain the route.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ENOS","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"},{"title":"Local memory","detail":"Recalls a sequence of events that shaped the camp’s reputation.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ENOS","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"],"baseline":true,"era":"1980 film only"}],"gear":[{"name":"Oil-supply truck","type":"Work vehicle","detail":"Provides Annie’s first ride; do not confuse it with the later killer’s vehicle.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ENOS","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}],"costume":"Original diner and truck stills show Enos in a work cap, short-sleeved blue work shirt and dark quilted vest.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-ENOS","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-barry":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["At the 1958 camp gathering Barry and Claudette share a flirtation, then leave the singing group for privacy in a storage area. His life before that night is not developed on screen."],"role":["At the 1958 camp gathering Barry and Claudette share a flirtation, then leave the singing group for privacy in a storage area. His life before that night is not developed on screen.","When someone enters, Barry reacts as if he has been caught breaking a rule, not as if he has met an unknown monster. He tries to explain away what they are doing, but is stabbed. Claudette is then left facing the attacker.","The pair’s murders become part of the camp’s history recounted years later. Although Mrs. Voorhees blames inattentive counselors for Jason’s 1957 death, this film does not establish that Barry personally supervised Jason or caused the drowning."],"status":"Killed in the 1958 prologue","abilities":[],"gear":[],"costume":"In the 1958 prologue, Barry wears a yellow Camp Crystal Lake shirt, white belt, navy shorts, light crew socks and muted canvas shoes.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-BARRY","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}},"friday13-claudette":{"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical":{"background":["She participates in the camp’s 1958 singing gathering and flirts with Barry. The pair slip away, and their conversation hints at ordinary romantic uncertainty rather than a fully supplied personal backstory."],"role":["She participates in the camp’s 1958 singing gathering and flirts with Barry. The pair slip away, and their conversation hints at ordinary romantic uncertainty rather than a fully supplied personal backstory.","After Barry is attacked, Claudette backs away through the storage space and begs the intruder not to hurt her. The scene ends with the threat overwhelming her; the identity of the attacker remains concealed.","Her death and Barry’s are later remembered as the 1958 murders that helped create Camp Blood’s reputation. The film does not establish that she was responsible for Jason in the previous year or give a detailed independent account of how she knew his mother."],"status":"Killed in the 1958 prologue","abilities":[],"gear":[],"costume":"In the 1958 prologue, Claudette wears a light-yellow Camp Crystal Lake shirt, navy shorts, a white belt and a wristwatch. The inspected original-film stills also show a headband, light socks and canvas camp shoes.","sourceIds":["F13-CHAR-CLAUDETTE","F13-CREDITS","F13-DIALOGUE"]}}}},"filmCards":[{"id":"friday-the-13th-1980-theatrical","title":"Friday the 13th","year":"1980","cover":"movie-covers/friday-the-13th-1980.jpg"}]};
const roster=window.COMIC_VAULT_CHARACTERS;
if(!Array.isArray(roster)||data.characters.length!==16)throw new Error('Friday the 13th requires the complete core roster and16 new character dossiers.');
